    {
      "id": "yo62wvj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. List of Fundamental Rights"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Part III of the Constitution (Articles 12 to 35) guarantees Fundamental Rights to all citizens, inspired by the American Bill of Rights.",
        "Articles 14–18 ensure Equality before Law, prohibition of discrimination, equality of opportunity, and abolition of untouchability and titles.",
        "Articles 19–22 safeguard freedoms including speech, assembly, association, movement, residence, profession, and protection of life and personal liberty.",
        "Article 21A makes free and compulsory education a Fundamental Right for children aged 6 to 14.",
        "Article 32 provides the Right to Constitutional Remedies, empowering citizens to move the Supreme Court directly for enforcement of rights."
      ],
      "id": "j16qb0d"
    },
